---
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import { courses } from "../content/courses";
import { legalPages } from "../content/legal";
import { site } from "../config/site";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { enquiryAction, pageCrumbs } from "../lib/links";

const crumbs = pageCrumbs([{ label: legalPages.privacy.label, href: legalPages.privacy.href }]);
const sendsEnquiry = enquiryAction(site.enquiryEndpoint) !== null;
const courseNames = courses.map((course) => course.title).join(", ");
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="Example privacy policy for the Webco Essential demonstration. It describes the fictional enquiry form and states that this demo does not send or store what you type."
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <PageHero
    crumbs={crumbs}
    eyebrow="Example"
    title="Privacy policy"
    lede="Example text for this demonstration website. It describes the fictional training provider shown here. It is not legal advice, and it is not the privacy policy of a real business."
  />

  <Section id="who" title="Who this page is about" narrow={true}>
    <p>
      Webco Essential is the name of this demonstration. The trainer, the town and the contact details are fictional.
      Webco Media publishes the demonstration. That does not make Webco Media the training provider.
    </p>
    <p>
      A real provider would name the organisation responsible for personal data. This page cannot do that, because no
      real training business is operating this site. No company number, VAT number or registered office is shown,
      because none belongs to this fictional provider.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="enquiry" title="The enquiry form" band={true} narrow={true}>
    <p>The contact page asks for:</p>
    <ul class="prose-list">
      <li>Name</li>
      <li>
        Phone, if you enter one. It is required only when you choose phone
        {site.showWhatsApp ? " or WhatsApp" : ""} as the way to reply
      </li>
      <li>Email</li>
      <li>Course: {courseNames}, or not sure yet</li>
      <li>
        Preferred contact method: phone, email{site.showWhatsApp ? ", or WhatsApp" : ""}
      </li>
      <li>Message</li>
    </ul>
    {
      sendsEnquiry ? (
        <p>
          This copy of the site is set to post those fields to a configured form address. This project does not include
          that handler, so this page cannot say who would read the message, how long it would be kept, or where it would
          be stored. A live provider has to add that before the form is used.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          On this demonstration the form is not connected to a server. Submitting it does not send the message. Nothing
          you type is stored in a cookie or anywhere else on the site. The words stay in the form on your screen until
          you leave the page. A note on the form says the same thing.
        </p>
      )
    }
    <p>
      If you open the contact page from a course button, the address can include the course name so the form selects it
      for you. That is only so you do not have to choose it again. It is not saved.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="contact-routes" title="Phone, email and WhatsApp" narrow={true}>
    <p>
      The phone number on this site is {site.phoneDisplay}. The email address is {site.email}.
      {site.showWhatsApp ? ` The WhatsApp number is ${site.whatsappDisplay}.` : ""}
      These are placeholders. {site.location.town} and {site.location.county} are placeholders too.
    </p>
    <p>
      Choosing a phone link, an email link or a WhatsApp link leaves this website and opens the app on your device.
      This site does not receive that call, email or chat, and it does not keep a copy.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="not-collected" title="What this site does not do" band={true} narrow={true}>
    <ul class="prose-list">
      <li>It does not ask you to create an account</li>
      <li>It does not take payment</li>
      <li>It does not add you to a mailing list</li>
      <li>It does not run analytics or advertising</li>
      <li>The reviews are sample text, not comments collected from learners</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The <a href={legalPages.cookies.href}>cookie policy</a> says what this website stores on your device.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="hosting" title="Serving the pages" narrow={true}>
    <p>
      The pages are static files. This project does not run a database. Whoever hosts a copy of the site may keep
      ordinary server logs, such as an IP address and the page requested. This demonstration does not name a host,
      because that depends on where a copy is published.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="rights" title="Rights, as an example" band={true} narrow={true}>
    <p>
      People in the UK have rights over personal data a real organisation holds, including access, correction, deletion,
      restriction and objection, and the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office. This demonstration
      does not hold enquiry records, so there is nothing here to retrieve or delete.
    </p>
    <p>
      The contact details above are fictional. They are not a route to a real privacy contact. A live provider replaces
      this page with their own notice, including who to write to and how long they keep an enquiry.
    </p>
    <p>
      Also see the <a href={legalPages.cookies.href}>cookie policy</a> and the
      <a href={legalPages.terms.href}>website terms</a>.
    </p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
